<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Ling of Chu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 529 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Ling of Chu (died 529 BCE) was a ruler of the State of Chu who seized the throne in 541 BCE by murdering his nephew, the reigning king. Ambitious and extravagant, he built the lavish Zhanghua Terrace, held a great interstate assembly and annexed the states of Chen and Cai. A rebellion led by his brothers in 529 BCE deserted him while he was on campaign, and he hanged himself.</p></div>
